id: pm-web-2ut6
title: Spanish (es) locale for package-owned UI strings
description: "Add a Spanish (es) locale catalog for the package-owned SPA UI strings (auth, nav, banners, settings, consent, dialog, error mapping). Register es in locale resolution and the settings language selector (English/Deutsch/Espanol). Legal pages remain an operator concern and are not translated by this package."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: es,i18n,locale,settings
created_at: "2026-07-17T06:52:56.558Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:24:58.701Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:24:58.700Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: es.json catalog exists with all 110 en keys translated to natural Spanish (usted register); es registered in SUPPORTED_LOCALES and resolveLocale (es and es-MX prefix match); settings language selector offers English/Deutsch/Espanol; npm run typecheck && npm run build && npm test green; catalog-parity test covers es automatically
release: 2026.7.17-1
resolution: "Work completed and released in 2026.7.17-1. Release attribution verified by containment rather than by date: git merge-base --is-ancestor c46797f v2026.07.17-1 succeeds, so 2026.7.17-1 is the first release whose tree holds the implementing commit. An earlier revision of this record said 2026.7.18; that came from matching the item's last-activity DATE to a release and is superseded."
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.7.17-1 heading, the first release actually containing c46797f, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Before this closeout the item had remained in_progress with no activity since its work shipped, so the delivery was missing from the changelog while still being counted as open work in every fleet audit. Closing it with an explicit release attribution is what added the historical entry."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T23:17:11.031Z",claude-code,"Release attribution corrected to 2026.7.17-1 after review. The first attribution used the item's last-activity DATE, which is unsound: an item can be touched before the release that finally carried its code. Verified instead by tag containment — git tag --contains c46797f reports 2026.7.17-1 as the first release holding the implementation commit. Greptile caught this on PR #67 by noticing a historical release predating its implementation."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the Spanish locale was completed and released in 2026.7.17-1, verified by tag containment against implementing commit c46797f. The item was never closed and sat in progress ever since, inflating every fleet audit."
body: ""
